\ manifest.fam — snapshots to serve (docs/NODE.md, step 10), after
\ proofs.fam and before connect.fam: tabminer's take_snapshot and the
\ name buckets behind it (miner/src/chain.rs, names.rs), so peers fast-sync
\ from the node.  The manifest after each block connected is kept for the
\ undo window: the output counter, the output parts (subtrees of the
\ state tree holding 1 to 2^14 unspent outputs, each one's parent more:
\ their level, index, count and root), the name trie's root, and each
\ name part's first key and hash; kept as changes from the parent's
\ (below), served as net.rs's encode_manifest.
\
\ The name parts come from the buckets (a key's top 16 bits), each kept
\ at 'B' and the bucket (2 bytes): its records' count and hash_domain 12
\ of the count and their bytes packed (as snap.fam checks them); the
\ buckets a block changes (rtouch) hashed again before its manifest.  A
\ part: buckets in order while their records are at most 4,096 (one
\ larger alone); its first key its first bucket's start, its hash
\ hash_domain 11 of each bucket and its hash.
\
\ minit  its buffers (stinit calls it).
\ mbuckets  the buckets noted (rtouch; all if rtall) hashed again.
\ msnap ( h lo hi u -- )  the manifest after block h (the counter: 40
\ bits), from its parent's and its undo record u (0: from the outputs, as
\ after a snapshot).
\ mread ( h -- a n | 0 0 )  block h's manifest, if kept and served
\ (malloc'd), as encode_manifest.
\ mdrop ( h -- )  block h's manifest dropped.

: kman  kb @ 5 lit + 2 lit be!  kb @ 1 lit + 4 lit be!  4D lit kb @ c!  7 lit ;   \ ( h chunk -- klen )
: kbkt  kb @ 1 lit + 2 lit be!  42 lit kb @ c!  3 lit ;                          \ ( b -- klen )
: mrb variable ;  : mrn variable ;  : mrc variable ;  : mrk variable ;  : mhb variable ;  : mb variable ;  : mpk variable ;
: mo variable ;  : mop variable ;  : mgb variable ;  : mgn variable ;  : mgc variable ;  : mgf variable ;  : mtmp variable ;
: mhh variable ;  : mdn variable ;  : mnp variable ;  : mrch variable ;
: mtp variable ;  : mch variable ;
:M MRBN 40000 lit ;                            \ a bucket's records' bytes, at most
:M MNAMES 40000 lit ;                          \ the name parts' bytes in a manifest, at most (5,577 parts: 22 million names)

: minit
mrb @ 0= if
	MRBN malloc mrb !  MRBN 3 lit / 2 lit lshift 10 lit + malloc mpk !
	40 lit alloc mtmp !  40 lit alloc mhh !  40 lit alloc mhb !  10000 lit malloc mgb !
	30 lit alloc mtp !  FFFFFFFF lit mch !
then ;

\ mcanon, ( m -- )  8 Montgomery words at m, as 32 canonical bytes at mop.
: mcanon,  8 lit 0 lit do dup i w@ fromm mop @ i 2 lit lshift + ! loop drop  mop @ 20 lit + mop ! ;
: m32,  mop @ !  mop @ 4 lit + mop ! ;                \ ( x -- )
\ mzero ( a n -- )  n bytes of zeros.
: mzero  ?dup if 0 lit do 0 lit over i + c! loop then drop ;

\ mbhash ( b -- )  bucket b hashed again from its records (dropped if none).
: mbhash
dup mb !  0 lit mrn !  0 lit mrc !
\ its records, in key order, their bytes one after another in mrb
72 lit kb @ c!  mb @ kb @ 1 lit + 2 lit be!  kb @ 3 lit + D lit mzero
10 lit
begin
	knext dup 10 lit = if drop kb2 @ c@ 72 lit =  kb2 @ 1 lit + 2 lit be@ mb @ = and else drop 0 lit then
while
	kb2 @ kb @ 10 lit bcopy
	mrn @ 200 lit + MRBN u< if
		10 lit mrb @ mrn @ + 200 lit sget  dup 0< if drop else mrn @ + mrn !  mrc @ 1 lit + mrc ! then
	then
	10 lit
repeat
mb @ kbkt
mrc @ if
	mrc @ tom mpk @ !
	mrb @ mrn @ mpk @ 4 lit + pack3
	mpk @ mrn @ 2 lit + 3 lit / 1 lit +  C lit  mhb @ 4 lit + hdom
	mrc @ mhb @ !  mhb @ 24 lit sput
else sdel then ;

\ mball  every bucket dropped, then each with records hashed again.
: mball
42 lit kb @ c!  kb @ 1 lit + 2 lit mzero
3 lit begin knext dup 3 lit = if drop kb2 @ c@ 42 lit = else drop 0 lit then while
	kb2 @ kb @ 3 lit bcopy  3 lit sdel  3 lit
repeat
72 lit kb @ c!  kb @ 1 lit + F lit mzero  0 lit mdn !
begin
	mdn @ 0= if 10 lit knext 10 lit = if kb2 @ c@ 72 lit = else 0 lit then else 0 lit then
while
	kb2 @ 1 lit + 2 lit be@  dup mbhash
	\ on from the next bucket's start
	dup FFFF lit = if drop 1 lit mdn ! else
		1 lit + 72 lit kb @ c!  kb @ 1 lit + 2 lit be!  kb @ 3 lit + D lit mzero
	then
repeat ;

: mbuckets
rtall @ if mball else rtn @ ?dup if 0 lit do rtb @ i w@ mbhash loop then then
0 lit rtn !  0 lit rtall ! ;

\ mgclose  the name part gathered (mgb: mgn words, each bucket's index then
\ hash) written: its first key (its first bucket's start) and hash.
: mgclose
mgn @ 0= 0=  mop @ mo @ u< and if
	mgf @ mop @ 2 lit be!  mop @ 2 lit + D lit mzero  mop @ F lit + mop !
	mgb @ mgn @ B lit mtmp @ hdom  mtmp @ mcanon,
	mnp @ 1 lit + mnp !
then
0 lit mgn !  0 lit mgc ! ;
\ mmore ( b n -- )  bucket b (its n records, its hash at mtmp+4) in a part:
\ a new one if this one would pass 4,096 records.
: mmore
mtmp @ 4 lit + mhh @ 8 lit wcopy
mgn @ if mgc @ over + 1000 lit u> if mgclose then then
mgn @ 0= if over mgf ! then
mgc @ + mgc !
tom mgb @ mgn @ w!  mhh @ mgb @ mgn @ 1 lit + 2 lit lshift + 8 lit wcopy  mgn @ 9 lit + mgn ! ;

\ ── Output parts (tabminer's Manifest, OutputLayout) ──
\
\ A part in memory, 30 bytes: its level, index (two words: the second 0),
\ count, root (8 canonical words). The parts after a block are made from
\ its parent's: a subtree the block did not touch keeps its parts; one it
\ did is counted again, from the parent's counts and the block's changes
\ (its outputs, from its first position to the counter; the positions it
\ emptied, from its undo record), or from the outputs where it lay within
\ a parent's part. A subtree holding more than 2^14 outputs is split.
:M MK 4000 lit ;

: mob variable ;  : mon variable ;  : mos variable ;  : mold variable ;   \ the parent's parts, their sums
: mnb variable ;  : mnn variable ;  : mncap variable ;                     \ the new ones
: mcb variable ;  : mcn variable ;                       \ the last made, kept (height)
: mea variable ;  : men variable ;                                          \ the emptied positions
: mml variable ;  : mmh variable ;  : mnl variable ;  : mnh variable ;     \ first made, the counter
: wfl variable ;  : wfh variable ;  : wel variable ;  : weh variable ;     \ the subtree's range
: mlo variable ;  : mhi variable ;  : mwi variable ;  : mec variable ;  : mmd variable ;
: mbl variable ;  : mbh variable ;  : mt0 variable ;  : mt1 variable ;  : mcn2 variable ;
: ma0 variable ;  : ma1 variable ;  : mb0 variable ;  : mb1 variable ;  : mse variable ;
: mu variable ;  : mxa variable ;  : mxn variable ;  : mss variable ;  : msp variable ;
: mrh variable ;  : mok variable ;  : mpi variable ;  : mj variable ;  : mat variable ;  : mfr variable ;  : mgo variable ;

\ p40 ( level index -- lo hi )  a subtree's first position (40 bits).
: p40
over 20 lit u< if
	2dup swap lshift  -rot  20 lit rot - rshift
else
	swap 20 lit - lshift 0 lit swap
then ;
\ p< ( alo ahi blo bhi -- flag )  a below b (40 bits).
: p<  rot 2dup = if 2drop u< else u> nip nip then ;
\ p- ( alo ahi blo bhi -- n )  a less b, below 2^32.
: p-  rot 2drop - ;

: ope  30 lit * mob @ + ;                                \ ( k -- a )  the parent's part k
: opf  ope dup @ swap 4 lit + @ p40 ;                     \ ( k -- lo hi )  its first position
: ope2  ope dup @ swap 4 lit + @ 1 lit + p40 ;            \ ( k -- lo hi )  past its last
: mne  30 lit * mnb @ + ;                                 \ ( k -- a )  new part k
: mnf  mne dup @ swap 4 lit + @ p40 ;

\ ekey ( k -- lo hi )  emptied position k; e< ( i j -- flag ); eswap ( i j -- ).
: ekey  3 lit lshift mea @ + dup @ swap 4 lit + @ ;
: e<  swap ekey rot ekey p< ;
: eswap
3 lit lshift mea @ + swap 3 lit lshift mea @ +
2 lit 0 lit do over i w@ over i w@  3 lit pick i w!  over i w! loop 2drop ;
\ msift ( root end -- )  heapsort's sift down; msort  the emptied, ascending.
: msift
mse !
begin dup 1 lit lshift 1 lit + dup mse @ u< while
	dup 1 lit + mse @ u< if dup dup 1 lit + e< if 1 lit + then then
	2dup e< if 2dup eswap nip else 2drop mse @ then
repeat 2drop ;
: msort
men @ 1 lit u> if
	men @ 1 lit rshift begin dup while 1 lit - dup men @ msift repeat drop
	men @ begin dup 1 lit u> while 1 lit - 0 lit over eswap  0 lit over msift repeat drop
then ;
\ memp ( u -- )  the positions undo record u's block emptied: its inputs
\ and the commits it consumed (its name events of type 1), sorted.
: memp
dup @ 2 lit lshift 100 lit + malloc mea !  0 lit men !
dup 10 lit + @ ?dup if 0 lit do
	dup 14 lit + i 3 lit lshift + mea @ men @ 3 lit lshift + 8 lit bcopy  men @ 1 lit + men !
loop then
dup 10 lit + @ 3 lit lshift 14 lit + over +    ( u p )
begin dup 2 lit pick dup @ 2 lit lshift + u< while
	dup @ 1 lit = if dup 4 lit + mea @ men @ 3 lit lshift + 8 lit bcopy  men @ 1 lit + men ! then
	dup @ dup 1 lit = if drop 50 lit else dup 2 lit = if drop 14 lit else 3 lit = if 8C lit else 4 lit then then then +
repeat 2drop
msort ;
\ epp ( lo hi -- k )  the emptied positions below.
: epp
mt1 ! mt0 !  0 lit mbl !  men @ mbh !
begin mbl @ mbh @ u< while
	mbl @ mbh @ + 1 lit rshift
	dup ekey mt0 @ mt1 @ p< if 1 lit + mbl ! else mbh ! then
repeat mbl @ ;
\ molo ( -- k )  the parent's parts ending at or before the subtree's
\ first position; mohi ( -- k )  those starting before its end.
: molo
0 lit mbl !  mon @ mbh !
begin mbl @ mbh @ u< while
	mbl @ mbh @ + 1 lit rshift
	dup ope2 mt1 ! mt0 !  wfl @ wfh @ mt0 @ mt1 @ p< if mbh ! else 1 lit + mbl ! then
repeat mbl @ ;
: mohi
0 lit mbl !  mon @ mbh !
begin mbl @ mbh @ u< while
	mbl @ mbh @ + 1 lit rshift
	dup opf wel @ weh @ p< if 1 lit + mbl ! else mbh ! then
repeat mbl @ ;
\ wmade ( -- n )  the positions the block made in the subtree.
: wmade
wfl @ wfh @ mml @ mmh @ p< if mml @ mmh @ else wfl @ wfh @ then ma1 ! ma0 !
wel @ weh @ mnl @ mnh @ p< if wel @ weh @ else mnl @ mnh @ then mb1 ! mb0 !
ma0 @ ma1 @ mb0 @ mb1 @ p< if mb0 @ mb1 @ ma0 @ ma1 @ p- else 0 lit then ;
\ mcount ( -- n )  the outputs in the subtree, counted to 2^14 + 1.
: mcount
wfl @ wfh @ or if
	wfl @ if wfl @ 1 lit - wfh @ else FFFFFFFF lit wfh @ 1 lit - then 6F lit -rot kpos
else 6F lit kb @ c! 1 lit then
0 lit mcn2 !
begin
	knext dup 6 lit = if
		drop kb2 @ c@ 6F lit =  kb2 @ 2 lit + 4 lit be@ kb2 @ 1 lit + c@ wel @ weh @ p< and
	else drop 0 lit then
	mcn2 @ MK u> 0= and
while
	kb2 @ kb @ 6 lit bcopy  mcn2 @ 1 lit + mcn2 !  6 lit
repeat mcn2 @ ;

\ mapp ( a -- )  a part appended to the new ones (their room doubled
\ when full).
: mapp
mnn @ mncap @ = if
	mncap @ 1 lit lshift 40 lit max  dup 30 lit * malloc
	mnb @ over mnn @ 30 lit * bcopy  mnb @ ?dup if free then  mnb ! mncap !
then
mnb @ mnn @ 30 lit * + 30 lit bcopy  mnn @ 1 lit + mnn ! ;
\ mpart ( level index count -- )  a new part, its root from the tree.
: mpart
mtp @ C lit + !  2dup mtp @ 4 lit + !  mtp @ !  0 lit mtp @ 8 lit + !
mtmp @ nget
8 lit 0 lit do mtmp @ i w@ fromm mtp @ 10 lit + i w! loop
mtp @ mapp ;

\ mw ( level index -- )  the subtree's parts, appended.
: mw
2dup p40 wfh ! wfl !  2dup 1 lit + p40 weh ! wel !
molo mlo !  mohi mhi !
mhi @ mlo @ - 1 lit = if mlo @ ope @ 2 lit pick u> else 0 lit then mwi !
wel @ weh @ epp  wfl @ wfh @ epp -  mec !
wmade mmd !
mold @  mec @ mmd @ or 0= and  mwi @ 0= and if
	mhi @ mlo @ - ?dup if 0 lit do mlo @ i + ope mapp loop then  2drop
else
	mold @ 0= mwi @ or if mcount else  mos @ mhi @ w@ mos @ mlo @ w@ - mmd @ + mec @ - then
	dup MK u> if
		drop  over 1 lit - over 1 lit lshift mw  over 1 lit - over 1 lit lshift 1 lit + mw  2drop
	else ?dup if mpart else 2drop then then
then ;

\ ── Kept: whole, or as changes ──
\
\ At 'M', the height, the chunk (1 KiB each; the length at chunk FFFF):
\ whole (0) or as changes from the parent's (1); the counter (two words);
\ the name root (canonical); the name parts' count and the parts (as
\ encode_manifest has them: first key, hash); then, from a word boundary,
\ the output parts as splices of the parent's: their count, and each one's
\ index there, the parts it removes, the parts it puts in their place and
\ those (30 bytes each). Whole: one splice of every part. Whole every 64th
\ block, or when the parent's is not kept, so one is rebuilt from at most
\ 63; those below the oldest kept whole are dropped (mprune).

\ mrec ( h -- a | 0 )  block h's record (malloc'd).
: mrec
dup FFFF lit kman sbuf @ 4 lit sget 4 lit = if
	sbuf @ @ dup malloc  ( h n a )
	over 3FF lit + A lit rshift 0 lit do
		2 lit pick i kman  over i A lit lshift + 400 lit sget drop
	loop
	nip nip
else drop 0 lit then ;
\ mspl ( rec -- p )  its splices.
: mspl  dup 2C lit + @ 2F lit * 30 lit + 3 lit + FFFFFFFC lit and + ;
\ mcpy ( a n -- )  n parts from a, appended to mxa (mxn of them).
: mcpy  dup 30 lit *  mxa @ mxn @ 30 lit * +  swap rot  mxn @ + mxn !  bcopy ;
\ mapply ( rec -- )  mob (mon parts) with the record's splices applied.
: mapply
mspl dup @ mss !  4 lit + msp !
mon @  msp @  mss @ ?dup if 0 lit do dup 8 lit + @ rot + swap  dup 8 lit + @ 30 lit * C lit + + loop then drop
30 lit * 30 lit + malloc mxa !  0 lit mxn !  0 lit mpi !
msp @ mss @ ?dup if 0 lit do
	mpi @ ope over @ mpi @ - mcpy
	dup C lit + over 8 lit + @ mcpy
	dup @ over 4 lit + @ + mpi !
	dup 8 lit + @ 30 lit * C lit + +
loop then drop
mpi @ ope mon @ mpi @ - mcpy
mob @ ?dup if free then  mxa @ mob !  mxn @ mon ! ;
\ mrebuild ( h -- flag )  mob, mon: block h's parts, from the record kept
\ whole at or below it and the changes since.
: mrebuild
dup mrh !  0 lit mob !  0 lit mon !  -1 lit mok !
begin
	mrh @ 0 lit kman sbuf @ 400 lit sget 4 lit < if 0 lit mok ! 0 lit else sbuf @ @ then
	mok @ and  mrh @ 0= 0= and
while mrh @ 1 lit - mrh ! repeat
mok @ if mrh @ 0 lit kman sbuf @ 400 lit sget 4 lit < if 0 lit mok ! else sbuf @ @ if 0 lit mok ! then then then
mok @ if
	1 lit + mrh @ do mok @ if i mrec ?dup if dup mapply free else 0 lit mok ! then then loop
else drop then
mok @ ;
\ mparts ( h -- flag )  mob, mon: block h's parts (the last made, taken,
\ if they are h's).
: mparts
dup mch @ = mcb @ 0= 0= and if
	drop mcb @ mob !  mcn @ mon !  0 lit mcb !  FFFFFFFF lit mch !  -1 lit
else mrebuild then ;

\ msput ( r -- r' )  the output parts' splices at r: the new parts
\ against the parent's (tabminer's splices), or one of them all (mold 0).
: msput
mold @ 0= if
	1 lit over !  0 lit over 4 lit + !  0 lit over 8 lit + !  mnn @ over C lit + !
	10 lit +  mnb @ over mnn @ 30 lit * bcopy  mnn @ 30 lit * +
else
	dup mss !  4 lit +  0 lit mpi !  0 lit mj !  0 lit mt0 !
	begin mpi @ mon @ u< mj @ mnn @ u< or while
		mpi @ mon @ u< mj @ mnn @ u< and if mpi @ ope mj @ mne C lit wcmp 0= else 0 lit then
		if mpi @ 1 lit + mpi !  mj @ 1 lit + mj ! else
			\ a run of differences, until they agree again
			mpi @ mat !  mj @ mfr !  -1 lit mgo !
			begin mgo @  mpi @ mon @ u< mj @ mnn @ u< or  and while
				mpi @ mon @ u< mj @ mnn @ u< and if
					mpi @ ope mj @ mne C lit wcmp 0= if 0 lit mgo ! else
						mpi @ opf mj @ mnf p< if mpi @ 1 lit + mpi ! else
							mj @ mnf mpi @ opf p< if mj @ 1 lit + mj ! else mpi @ 1 lit + mpi !  mj @ 1 lit + mj ! then
						then
					then
				else mpi @ mon @ u< if mpi @ 1 lit + mpi ! else mj @ 1 lit + mj ! then then
			repeat
			mat @ over !  mpi @ mat @ - over 4 lit + !  mj @ mfr @ - over 8 lit + !
			C lit +  mfr @ mne over mj @ mfr @ - 30 lit * bcopy  mj @ mfr @ - 30 lit * +
			mt0 @ 1 lit + mt0 !
		then
	repeat
	mt0 @ mss @ !
then ;

\ mdrop ( h -- )  block h's record dropped.
: mdrop
dup mch @ = if mcb @ ?dup if free then  0 lit mcb !  FFFFFFFF lit mch ! then
dup FFFF lit kman sbuf @ 4 lit sget 4 lit = if
	sbuf @ @ 3FF lit + A lit rshift ?dup if 0 lit do dup i kman sdel loop then
	FFFF lit kman sdel
else drop then ;
\ mprune ( h -- )  with block h the tip, the records no longer needed:
\ those below the oldest served (h - 1,007), down to one kept whole, go
\ 64 at a time.
: mprune
3EF lit - dup 0< 0= over 3F lit and 0= and over 40 lit u< 0= and if
	dup 40 lit - do i mdrop loop
else drop then ;

: mrst variable ;  : mgvp variable ;  : mgvn variable ;
\ mgiven ( a n -- )  the next manifest's output parts these (a fast
\ sync's, checked), not counted again from the outputs.
: mgiven  mgvn ! mgvp ! ;
: msnap  ( h lo hi u -- )
mu ! mnh ! mnl ! mb !
\ the parent's parts, or none (counted from the outputs)
mu @ if mb @ 1 lit - mparts else 0 lit then mold !
mold @ 0= if mob @ ?dup if free then  0 lit mob !  0 lit mon ! then
mu @ if mu @ 4 lit + @ mml !  mu @ C lit + @ mmh !  mu @ memp else mnl @ mml !  mnh @ mmh !  0 lit mea !  0 lit men ! then
mon @ 1 lit + 2 lit lshift malloc mos !  0 lit mos @ 0 lit w!
mon @ ?dup if 0 lit do mos @ i w@ i ope C lit + @ + mos @ i 1 lit + w! loop then
0 lit mnn !
mgvp @ if mgvn @ ?dup if 0 lit do mgvp @ i 30 lit * + mapp loop then  0 lit mgvp ! else 27 lit 0 lit mw then
\ kept whole every 64th block
mb @ 3F lit and 0= if 0 lit mold ! then
mnn @ 3C lit * MNAMES + 80 lit + malloc dup mo ! mop !  mo @ mrst !
mold @ if 1 lit else 0 lit then m32,  mnl @ m32,  mnh @ m32,
mtmp @ troot  mtmp @ mcanon,
\ the name parts (their count written once known)
mop @ mhh @ 20 lit + !  0 lit m32,
0 lit mnp !  0 lit mgn !  0 lit mgc !
mrst @ 30 lit + MNAMES + 2F lit -  mo !     \ the limit, for mgclose
0 lit kbkt mtmp @ 24 lit sget 24 lit = if 0 lit mtmp @ @ mmore then
3 lit begin knext dup 3 lit = if drop kb2 @ c@ 42 lit = else drop 0 lit then while
	kb2 @ kb @ 3 lit bcopy  3 lit mtmp @ 24 lit sget drop
	kb2 @ 1 lit + 2 lit be@ mtmp @ @ mmore
	3 lit
repeat
mgclose
mnp @ mhh @ 20 lit + @ !
mop @ 3 lit + FFFFFFFC lit and  msput mop !
\ stored, in chunks
mrst @ mo !  mop @ mo @ - mrn !
mrn @ sbuf @ !  mb @ FFFF lit kman sbuf @ 4 lit sput
mo @ mop !  0 lit mrc !
begin mrn @ while
	mrn @ 400 lit u< if mrn @ else 400 lit then
	mb @ mrc @ kman mop @ 2 lit pick sput
	dup mop @ + mop !  mrn @ swap - mrn !  mrc @ 1 lit + mrc !
repeat
mo @ free
\ the new parts kept for the next block's
mcb @ ?dup if free then  mnb @ mcb !  mnn @ mcn !  mb @ mch !  0 lit mnb !  0 lit mncap !
mob @ ?dup if free then  0 lit mob !  mos @ free  mea @ ?dup if free then
mb @ mprune ;

\ mread ( h -- a n | 0 0 )  the manifest after block h, if kept, as
\ net.rs's encode_manifest (malloc'd): the counter, the output parts
\ (level, index, count, root), the name root, the name parts.
: mown variable ;  : mrr variable ;
: mread
dup mrec ?dup if
	mrr !
	dup mch @ = mcb @ 0= 0= and if drop mcb @ mob !  mcn @ mon !  0 lit mown !  -1 lit else mrebuild  -1 lit mown ! then
	if
		mon @ 2D lit *  mrr @ 2C lit + @ 2F lit * +  30 lit + dup malloc dup mo ! mop !
		mrr @ 4 lit + @ m32,  mrr @ 8 lit + @ m32,  mon @ m32,
		mon @ ?dup if 0 lit do
			i ope @ mop @ c!  i ope 4 lit + mop @ 1 lit + 2C lit bcopy  mop @ 2D lit + mop !
		loop then
		mrr @ C lit + mop @ 20 lit bcopy  mop @ 20 lit + mop !
		mrr @ 2C lit + @ m32,
		mrr @ 30 lit + mop @ mrr @ 2C lit + @ 2F lit * bcopy
		mo @ swap
	else 0 lit 0 lit then
	mown @ if mob @ ?dup if free then then  0 lit mob !
	mrr @ free
else drop 0 lit 0 lit then ;
